  "description": {
    "text": "The 2006 Gym Challenge was again a store representative match at Japan's Official Pokémon Card Gyms, picking each shop's players for the Gym Final in May 2006. Every player got eight basic Energy cards stamped ジム☆チャレンジ in the newest Energy design, now with Darkness and Metal, which had become basic Energy, beside the six types of the 2003 set. The top three of each store also got the special Darkness Energy with the same foil stamp, and the winner a silver Victory Medal: the 2005 medal reprinted, still with its 2005 copyright, with a ジム☆チャレンジ 2006 stamp in the text box. A silver medal with a 2006 copyright and no stamp is listed here too, though accounts differ on whether it was given in 2006 or 2007.\n\nIn December 2006 official gym events also traded Lucario 002/DP-P for the mount that CoroCoro Comic's Riolu 001/DP-P came on, while stocks lasted.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Japan Official Pokemon Card Gym Events 2003 - 2007",
